WEBVTT

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.660
A few days after our treasure hunt...

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.080
Oh, no! I totally forgot!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.410
Yutoria? What's wrong?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.410
You really have to ask?!
Since our treasure hunt was a failure,

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.580
we're no closer to paying off
the inheritance tax!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.370
Well, that's true...

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.290
Why aren't you at all concerned?!

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.750
At this rate, we'll go bankrupt
before we get the old man's legacy!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.790
And that's freaking you out?

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.660
I've got your money right here.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.790
Huh?

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.410
M-Marika?

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.500
It's 500,000 gold.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.120
This is your share of the profits.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.700
Wh-Where did you get all this money?

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.080
Don't tell me... You're a thief?! A burglar?!

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.790
Stop it! You'll tarnish my name!

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.450
Th-Then, where exactly...?

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:13.160
Remember those ghost-type maju I defeated?

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.620
Their bracers sold for a ton.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.700
I said I'd give you half,
so just take it already.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.450
For real?! Thank goodness!
We've done it, President!

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.750
With this much, we can hang on a little longer!

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.200
Your president here knew
they were worth something.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.830
He's the one who told me
to exchange 'em for gold.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:38.500
Is that true? Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.290
S-Sorry.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.540
Are your finances hurting that bad?

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.660
In that case, you can have my share too.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.750
--Huh?
--What?

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.620
What? Why are you making such weird faces?

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.330
Here.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.500
Y-You shouldn't...

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.290
It's fine.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.200
In exchange, could I ask you a favor?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.330
O-Of course! We'd be happy to help!

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.000
Then...

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.910
...I want you to let me work here.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.500
--Huh?
--What?

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.250
There you go with the faces again.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.040
I'm saying to make me an employee!

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.370
Huh? You're fine with that?

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.410
You'd be doing us a favor.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:30.950
I-I'm just saying, I had fun searching
for the treasure together.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:35.040
And I learned how my grandpa felt too.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.370
It really made me want to try working here!

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.620
Really? That would help!

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.830
As secretary, I'd love to have you!

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.200
Anyways, you can defer my salary
since you're out of money.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.450
I-I appreciate it.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.450
It's settled then.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.120
Glad to work with you.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.660
<i>Let's dive right into today's letters</i>

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.160
<i>It's "Personal Advice" and the title is</i>

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.160
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.790
<i>Hey, hear me out.</i>
<i>There's something I really wanna say</i>

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:36.000
<i>You've got courage to follow</i>
<i>your dreams which is why I chose you</i>

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.120
<i>Is it a risky bet</i>

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.580
<i>Despite no experience,</i>
<i>we jumped right in together</i>

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.040
<i>And this unpredictable story</i>

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:53.120
<i>Is your creation--</i>
<i>a heart-throbbing innovation</i>

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.580
<i>Quickly! Quickly! Take me along</i>

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.200
<i>On a bittersweet love venture</i>

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:03.040
<i>Ah! Measured not by skill</i>
<i>but by scale and romance</i>

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.080
<i>Hurry! Hurry! Boldly, subtly, show your appeal</i>

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.120
<i>Ah! Our meeting was a miracle</i>
<i>that can't be neglected</i>

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.700
<i>It's galactic level</i>

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.200
<i>I see. Sounds like you're head over heels.</i>

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.500
<i>Let's tell him, just like battle</i>

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.870
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.250
<i>Everyone, Hurry! Hurry Love! Love!!</i>

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.120
"Episode Five: New Employee"

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.410
Contract?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:42.540
That's right. We have to report
employee changes to the Agency.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:46.540
For that, an official contract
needs to be filed.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:49.790
I gave it to Marika to fill out, but...

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.040
Still haven't got it back?

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.870
By the way, when does it need to be filed?

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.370
Before tomorrow to get
processed by the deadline.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.410
Tomorrow, huh?
The thing is, Marika's on vacation today.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:08.580
Hey! Marika? You there?!

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.500
Marika! Come out if you're there!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.950
Is she out somewhere?

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.500
Hey! Marika!

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.330
--Whoa!
--Would you shut up already?!

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.620
What the--?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:31.410
--It's you, President! What are you doing?
--Ow, ow, ow...

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.370
Huh? Going somewhere?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:37.500
I came to get your contract
since you never gave it back.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.790
Oh, about that...

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.620
Don't tell me you lost it or--

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.950
I-I didn't! I just forgot where I put it!

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.660
Th-That's what we call losing something.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.910
This is...

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.120
It's a total mess in here...

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:05.040
Behold, my perfect arrangement!
Everything I want is within reach!

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.330
And how is that not a mess?

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:12.950
The contract, right?
If it's not here, it must be in storage.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.790
Why would it be there?

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:18.410
I think I put it away while
cleaning up grimoires.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.620
This way.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.450
I've got a bad feeling...

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.410
Go figure.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.750
There's nowhere to step in this sea of books.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.370
This way, President.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.660
R-Right.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.250
By the way, your grandpa
was a wizard too, right?

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.950
That's right. In fact, he was a famous,
seven-star adventurer!

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.660
Seven stars? That's amazing!

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:51.120
And since I have the same blood as him,
I'm just as much a genius!

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:57.370
Well, seeing as how we could use
your genius, let's find that contract.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.620
A-All right, already!

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.370
I think it's on that shelf.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:04.200
Oh! Found it!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.000
No way! It's a thief trap!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Huh?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.410
Ouch!

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.750
Where are we?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.000
The tunnels under town.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.660
The tunnels? But why are we here?

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.830
We were mistaken for invaders
and teleported here.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.450
You fell for a trap in your own house?

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.040
It's not my fault! It's one my grandpa made!

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.870
I haven't figured 'em all out yet!

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.290
In any case, let's hurry back.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.790
Obviously!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:53.160
Huh?

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.790
Wh-What's that?!

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.830
This is no normal tunnel!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.080
A mechanized dungeon?

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.370
Correct! At least, that's what
I heard from my friend Else.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:20.040
I guess a gate suddenly appeared out of nowhere!

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:24.120
They're not mushrooms!
Gates don't just sprout from the ground!

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.040
There's a whole dungeon and everything.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:32.660
But the inside was mechanized
and she was too scared to go farther.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:35.660
You sure she wasn't tricked by a maju?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.660
If there was a place like that,
I would know about it.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.870
But there's all sorts of rumors going around!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.830
Imperial even said they'll be exploring it soon!

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.290
What? Imperial did?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.750
If that's true, they're onto something.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:58.290
Hmph. I don't recall ever seeing
a dungeon here before.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.750
I wonder when it appeared?

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.160
The question is, are we really going inside?

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:09.700
Nobody gets the jump on me.
I live by the words, "First come, first served!"

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:13.580
Nobody really cares how
you live your life, though.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.500
Hey! Try caring about your coworkers!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.200
Studies show when people get along,
profits go through the--

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.370
This place sure is something else.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.160
It really does look mechanized.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:33.410
Tsk. I've never seen a dungeon like this before.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:38.540
This corruption has progressed pretty far...

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.450
I've never seen anything like this.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:49.040
There has to be a reason for it.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.830
You know, it's pretty obvious that
this place is weird, so let's leave and--

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.370
Eek! M-M-Mmm!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.120
Mmm?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.660
Mouse!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.450
W-Well, there's probably a few in these tunnels.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.500
I-I hate mice so much!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.290
That's more than a few!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.080
Y-You're crushing me!

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.370
Don't you dare leave my side
or I'll use attack magic on you!

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:18.580
You would?

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.330
Just promise me!

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:24.500
She's actually afraid.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.950
She's finally acting her age...

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:32.580
Wh-What's that look for? You're making fun!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.790
I-I am not!

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:38.700
Where the heck are they coming from?!
There're mice everywhere!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.370
Huh? It's like they're running from something...

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.830
I guess I'll just have to
wipe 'em out with magic!

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:52.660
W-Wait up a sec!
There might be flammable gas in here!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:55.040
And aren't we under the city?!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:58.200
Ugh! I just wanna get out of here!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:02.830
I bet if we follow the mice,
they'll lead us to an exit. Just relax and--

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:06.290
Huh?! There's no way in hell
I'm walking with mice!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:09.410
Our other option is staying here forever.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.000
Carry me then.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:13.660
Huh?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:17.000
Carry me on your back! It's an emergency!

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.790
An emergency, huh?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:24.660
Hmph! Just do as I say and all will be fine.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.660
Wow! Your back is easy to ride on.
I'm impressed.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.790
Well, thanks.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.870
That doesn't please me one bit.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.910
What the--?

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:43.080
This is worse than corruption.
This entire place feels abnormal.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.250
Is this as deep as it goes?

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:49.830
Having come this far,
it'd be nice to leave with something.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:53.500
There has to be something.
My instincts tell me so.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.750
You say for that every dungeon we visit.
And you're usually wrong.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.830
You win some, you lose some.
It's all the luck of the draw.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.450
Do you even know what that means?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:13.000
Whoa, check it out! It's rare-earth!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:17.290
Now we're talking!
First come, first served, baby!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.250
The thing is, I think we have company.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.290
What?!

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.500
Tsk! Maju, huh?

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:35.450
Huh?

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.790
Marika, it's the exit!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:38.830
Marika?

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.040
She fell asleep.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.750
That big scare tired her out.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.330
President... Get me some snacks...

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.750
She bosses me around, even in dreams...

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.500
Anyways, what is this anomaly?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.580
I have a bad feeling about it...

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:08.450
Really? All that happened?

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.580
Yeah.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.790
It's been a wild day, huh?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:12.910
Thanks.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.660
I'm curious about the anomaly.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.080
We should probably look into it.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:21.830
Yeah. I'm just glad neither of us were hurt.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:28.120
Now I'm exhausted.
Getting her contract turned into an ordeal.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.330
So? Where's the contract?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.500
Uh... In Marika's house...

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.370
Everyone, big trouble!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:38.370
I-I'm sorry! I'll get it right away!

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:41.200
Um, what are you talking about?

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.410
Huh? The contract, right?

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:46.290
Oh... This isn't about that.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.790
Rivar from Cyedge was
apparently hurt in a dungeon!

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.250
Rivar was?

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:55.910
Yes, and he'll be out of commission for months.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:14:00.580
I know his personality stinks,
but he's supposed to be pretty skilled.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.950
From what I heard, he had a mishap
clearing a strange dungeon.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.660
A strange dungeon?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:11.870
Oh! Maybe it's the same weird
tunnel the president was in!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:18.040
Speaking of which, I've heard people
are finding weird dungeons all over.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.580
The insides look corrupted and mechanized...

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:24.540
...and there's maju nobody's ever seen.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:29.620
I think the anomaly he saw in the tunnel
is somehow connected.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:32.290
What do you think is happening?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:38.290
In order to find out more,
I think it's best if we talk to Rivar ourselves.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.830
You're right. As much as I hate it.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.410
We need to get to the bottom of this.
As much as I hate it.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:48.290
I'll come too! As much as I hate it.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:52.700
I'll stay here and hold the fort!
As much as I hate it!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.790
What an awful thing to say.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.910
Um, excuse me?

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.910
Yes, can I help you?

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.870
Um, we're here to see Rivar.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.500
Have you scheduled a visit?

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.620
No, we haven't.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:13.450
I'm terribly sorry, but we can't
allow unscheduled visits.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.660
It's fine, we know the guy!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.700
Even if you do,
we don't allow unscheduled visits.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.200
With you, it's "Schedule this! Schedule that!"

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.700
We know the guy, so who cares?!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.120
It's the rules. I'm sorry.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.750
Excuse me?! You're so stubborn!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.790
Oh, my. Long time no see.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.200
You're...

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.700
Valmi?

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.870
Not since the contest, right?
Is life treating all of you well?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.330
Yup, thank you.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.500
That's wonderful to hear!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.450
So? What brings you here?

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:50.620
Actually, we heard that Rivar got hurt.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:54.250
Yes! He was bruised, battered,
and beaten to a pulp!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:58.250
His big nose was broken too,
so that's good news!

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.660
R-Right...

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:03.700
We want to see Rivar and hear
what he has to say, but...

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.540
That's fine by me! He's this way.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.040
Um, they haven't scheduled a visit!

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:14.370
That's fine. Just treat them
like they're guests of mine.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:15.450
But...

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.160
Pretty please?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.830
I'm afraid I can't...

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.080
Pretty please?

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.660
I-It's the rules!

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:27.000
Please don't make me say it again.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:31.080
G-Go on ahead!

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.790
It's right this way.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:39.330
Shit! Why'd this happen to me?

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.540
I never should've gone to that dungeon!

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.080
Coming in!

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.790
Excuse us.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.000
Wh-What do you guys want?!

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.580
They came to visit you.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.620
I-I never asked for that!

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:59.410
Hey! That's no way to talk
to people worried about you!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:05.040
Worried? Hmph, I know better!
You Kibou guys were just bored!

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.700
You're unbelievable.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:13.080
Anyways, what happened?
We heard you went in a strange dungeon.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.580
That's...

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:18.540
I saw something unusual
in a tunnel under the city.

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.660
Like it was corrupted...

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:22.080
Say what?!

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:26.500
I think something strange
is happening in Gatepia.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.040
So be it. I'll tell you.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:37.450
Valmi and I went to explore
a dungeon that recently appeared.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:43.450
It was lifeless and mechanized with tons
of precious metals deep inside.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:47.160
Precious metals? You mean, rare-earth?

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:53.290
Yeah, precisely. But there were
all these maju I've never seen before.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.330
You metal muppet!

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.950
That didn't hurt at all!

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:07.950
Can we go home now? We're outnumbered here.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:13.330
Shuddap! This is our chance!
Nothing something, nothing gained!

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:18.540
If you don't know how it goes,
please don't use fancy words!

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.950
Just watch this!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:29.200
That's what happens when I get serious!
You wanna piece of...?

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.750
Wh-What?!

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:45.620
When I came to, I was here in the infirmary.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:49.950
Yeah? It's impressive you escaped in one piece.

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.330
W-Well...

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:56.120
It's because I carried him out!
He was ridiculously heavy!

00:18:56.120 --> 00:19:00.540
Th-That's a trade secret!
You're giving the company a bad rap!

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:04.200
It's your fault for rushing
into battle like that.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.580
You should be groveling
on all fours thanking me.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.000
You're the one who didn't support me!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.370
Did I not help you recover
from the verge of death?

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:17.700
Hmph.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:22.660
So there you have it.
Rivar was thoroughly beat and humiliated.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.290
I see. That makes sense.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:26.500
Huh?! Don't believe that!

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.540
Now we know what happened,
but that doesn't explain the anomaly.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:34.580
We can't afford to ignore it.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.580
We can't ignore what?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:42.580
All that precious rare-earth!
We could pay off the inheritance tax with it!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:47.250
True. And I've heard the price
of rare-earth is on the rise!

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:51.160
Then let's go check it out!
I'm sure we can manage it!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.750
Let's do it, President!

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.580
Hmm... It sounds quite dangerous, but...

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:59.200
...should we give it a shot?

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:02.120
To get my dad's legacy once and for all.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.580
That's more like it!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:07.950
C'mon. Let's head back to the office and prep.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.500
Wait.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.000
What? You actually look serious for a change.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.410
I'm afraid I can't let you go.

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:17.120
Huh?! Why not?!

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.370
Look what happened to me.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:23.410
Small fry like you guys don't stand a chance.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.330
You'll get hurt for nothing.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.790
You don't know that for sure!
We're nothing like you!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:32.330
That's right! We're going in fully prepared!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.370
R-Relax, you two!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.120
You won't listen to me?

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:39.660
Nope! We've made up our mind!

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.830
Very well.

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:45.790
In that case, you'll have to
defeat me first if--

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.700
What'd you expect?
You're broken from head to toe.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:56.330
Looks like you defeated yourself.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.000
Shit! You guys will pay for this!

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:01.250
But we didn't do anything.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:06.950
Well, seeing how insistent he is,
let's take lots of preparation.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.910
Get well soon.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.790
I wonder if they'll come back alive.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.870
You were worried enough to stop them?

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:23.660
You do have a good side to you.
Too bad you were so uncool.

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:26.500
Shut up. It's not like that.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:30.250
I seriously don't think they can handle it.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.540
Well, let's just leave it at that!

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:40.200
All right, we're good to go!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:43.750
Yup! I packed a bunch of medicine too!

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:48.620
It's my first dungeon as an employee.
I'll show you the power of magic!

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:54.040
Great! Let's get our hands on that
rare-earth and make the legacy ours!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.040
Right!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:58.250
Let's go, guys!

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:02.250
Um, one thing before you go...

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:04.580
What's the matter, Guide?

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:07.910
Remember the contract that's due today?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:09.080
Uh...

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:10.830
It's still in Marika's house.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:14.700
President... Run!

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:16.040
Huh?

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:17.540
Run!

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:19.370
Wha--?!

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:43.250
<i>Looking way up into the night sky</i>

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:47.870
<i>A pretty jewel caught my eye</i>

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:52.200
<i>Clear skies tomorrow sure would be nice</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:56.330
<i>Now, make a wish upon a star</i>

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:58.410
<i>Lazily</i>

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:01.250
<i>Today comes to a close</i>

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:05.620
<i>Dead tired and worn out</i>

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:12.120
<i>Good work</i>
<i>Let's do our best again tomorrow</i>

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.700
<i>Goodnight</i>

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.870
<i>Every day is sparkling</i>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:21.410
<i>Just like a box of jewels (sparkling)</i>

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.620
<i>And so brilliant</i>

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.830
<i>Any work undone</i>

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:30.410
<i>We'll leave for dreamland (sleep tight)</i>

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:33.910
<i>Let's embark on adventure</i>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:38.200
<i>So sleep soundly tonight</i>

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:43.450
<i>And meet up with me in our dreams</i>

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:46.540
<i>Sleep tight</i>
